pocket-motion-only: an exposure renders one frame N times and averages the rasters, which is a delivered film's cost and a delivered film's look; every upstream target presents to a live display one tick per frame, at a rate the display sets, where N rasters per frame is time the PSP GE, the ESP32 and the browser host do not have and a display does not show.

0034 — a shutter: one frame rendered as an exposure, the average of N
renders with every playing baked timeline's transform tracks evaluated
between ticks. The design is `docs/shutter.design.md` in this repository;
the prototype it was measured on is `baselines/shutter/prototype.diff`.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `engine/core/src/shutter.rs` (new): `integrates` (translate X/Y/Z,
  scale, scaleX/Y, rotate, rotateX/Y, skewX — every one paint-time),
  `value_at` (the expression `tick_timelines` evaluates), and `sampled`,
  which takes a track at `tc + num/den` ticks. Between two ticks it is the
  segment's own eased curve, only where the realm shows that motion in
  progress; a zero-length keyframe interval, a one-tick segment, a
  fill-less start or end, a choreography loop wrap and an iteration wrap
  whose ends differ (rotations compare modulo 360) are jumps, and a sample
  never crosses one: it clamps to the tick on the frame's side.
- `engine/core/src/lib.rs`: `Ui::shutter_sample(num, den)` folds the
  integrated tracks of every playing timeline the way `tick_timelines`
  folds them and writes `anim_values`. No clock moves and no relayout is
  marked. `num = 0` writes back what the tick wrote. A node whose style
  carries `shutter-hold` is skipped; the flag is not inherited.
- `engine/core/src/anim.rs`: `ease` is crate-visible.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: `resolve_shutter_hold` (style and overrides).
- `contracts/spec/spec.ts` and the generated `spec.rs`, microts
  `spec.rs` and `component-types-microts.ts`: prop `shutterHold` (198,
  int, not animatable, not layout-dirtying). 198 because `0027` took 183
  (`arcCap`), `0029` 184 (`gradShape`) and `0033` 185-186 (`glowMode`,
  `glowThreshold`), and the vector-paths design has pencilled thirteen
  props after the last one allocated.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: the `shutter-hold` utility.
- `engine/wasm/src/lib.rs`: `ui_render_exposure(scale, spanNum, spanDen,
  samples)` renders sample k at `span * (2k + 1 - n) / 2n` ticks (centred,
  exact in i64), accumulates straight-alpha RGBA as premultiplied u32 sums
  (simd128, the scalar loop's bytes), writes the tick's values back, walks
  the DrawList once more so it and the inspector latch are the frame's,
  and resolves `a = (2Σa + n) / 2n`, `c = (2Σca + Σa) / 2Σa`, rounding half
  up. `samples <= 1` or a zero span is `ui_render_scaled`.
  `ui_draw_hash_exposure` folds the per-sample DrawList hashes.
  `ui_exposure_reserve(scale)` sizes the scratch before a host's first
  snapshot, and `ui_exposure_scratch_ptr`/`_len` name it so a snapshot can
  skip it. `ui_shutter_sample` is for a host that renders the samples
  itself (the reference test does).
- `hosts/web/wasm-ops.js`: `renderExposure`, `drawHashExposure`,
  `reserveExposure`, `exposureScratch`. The first three throw on a wasm
  without the export rather than falling back to an unblurred render.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`: offset 0 writes back the tick across every
  jump shape and a comma list; a sample inside a segment; each jump; a
  spin through its wraps; opacity and width held while translate moves;
  the hold, at the style and at the override layer, not inherited;
  `value_at` against `tick_timelines` at every clock.
- `tests/tailwind.test.ts`: `shutter-hold` compiles to the flag alone.

Red cases, each a one-line edit to the patch, each turning the named core
test red and nothing else: a one-tick segment read as motion (`len < 1`),
the right tick's value not checked against the segment's end, rotations
not compared modulo 360, a fill-less start or end read as a constant, the
choreography loop wrap not treated as a jump, the hold flag ignored, and
opacity or width added to `integrates`.

